  "notes": "つるつる is a mimetic word that works as both {擬態語|ぎたいご} (describing smoothness) and {擬音語|ぎおんご} (describing the sound of slurping noodles).\n\nSENSE 1 — SMOOTH/SLIPPERY:\n- つるつる{滑|すべ}る: to slide/slip smoothly\n- つるつるの{肌|はだ}: smooth skin\n- つるつるの{頭|あたま}: bald head\n- つるつるになる: to become smooth/slippery\n\nSENSE 2 — SLURPING:\n- つるつる{食|た}べる: to slurp (noodles)\n- つるつると{啜|すす}る: to slurp up\nUsed specifically for noodle-like foods: うどん, そば, ラーメン, そうめん.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- すべすべ: smooth to the touch (pleasant texture, e.g., skin)\n- ぬるぬる: slimy, slippery (unpleasant, e.g., seaweed)\n- さらさら: smooth and flowing (e.g., hair, sand)",
